      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Suspected duplicate of: https://feedback.vrchat.com/bug-reports/p/youtube-videos-fail-to-load-frequently\n\n@{69b1bee195d05cb7407bc20e|full_name} This bug report is missing reproduction steps and information about the error message, and as such is not actionable (yet). It seems like you may have posted a support request publicly to the incorrect channel. Can you reproduce the issue and attach [output logs](https://help.vrchat.com/hc/en-us/articles/9521522810899-Where-do-I-find-my-Output-Logs-and-Crash-Dumps)?\n\nNot helpful: \"I can't play a video\" - but what did you try to do, and what did you expect? No steps to reproduce your issue and to be helped, it reads like a complaint or a support requests on a public bug report forum and doesn't signal what's wrong or what you want to be done about it.\n\nHelpful: \"I tried playing URL https://example.com/ in several worlds ([list of worlds]) using both AVPro and Unity Video players and I received error XYZ with [AVPro/Unity Video/both]. Output logs are attached. My yt-dlp version is [version]. I [can/can't] download the video using yt-dlp [version number of the latest release] from the upstream project.\" - triage, steps to reproduce.\n\nFor isolated issues or customer support visit https://help.vrchat.com/\n\n- https://help.vrchat.com/hc/en-us/articles/1500002378742-I-m-having-issues-with-video-players-in-VRChat",
